---
layout: base.njk
title: Dataset
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/papaparse.min.js
  - /assets/js/xlsx.full.min.js
  - /assets/js/plotly-2.20.0.min.js
extraBodyScripts:
  - /assets/js/data-view.js
---
<div class="container">
<div class="card-body">

  <p><a href="/data/">&larr; Your Datasets</a></p>

  <div id="dv-loading" class="alert alert-info">Loading dataset&hellip;</div>
  <div id="dv-error" class="alert alert-danger" hidden></div>

  <div id="dv-content" hidden>
    <div class="d-flex flex-row bd-highlight mb-3 align-items-start justify-content-between">
      <div style="margin-right:1em;">
        <h2 id="dv-name"></h2>
        <p id="dv-summary" class="text-muted"></p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-success text-nowrap" id="dv-create-study">Create study</a>
    </div>

    <div id="dv-scan-progress" class="alert alert-info" hidden></div>

    <ul class="nav nav-tabs mb-3" id="dv-tabs" role="tablist">
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link active" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-table" type="button">Table</button></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-columns" type="button">Columns</button></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-univariate" type="button">Univariate</button></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-bivariate" type="button">Bivariate</button></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-treatment" type="button">Covariate balance</button></li>
      <li class="nav-item"><button class="nav-link" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#tab-correlations" type="button">Correlations</button></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="tab-content">

      <!-- Table -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="tab-table" role="tabpanel">
        <div class="row mb-3 align-items-end">
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-table-search">Search / filter rows</label>
            <input type="text" class="form-control" id="dv-table-search" placeholder="Matches any column, as text" />
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-table-sort1">Sort by</label>
            <div class="d-flex gap-1">
              <select class="form-select" id="dv-table-sort1"><option value="">(none)</option></select>
              <select class="form-select w-auto" id="dv-table-sort1-dir"><option value="asc">&uarr;</option><option value="desc">&darr;</option></select>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-table-sort2">Then by</label>
            <div class="d-flex gap-1">
              <select class="form-select" id="dv-table-sort2"><option value="">(none)</option></select>
              <select class="form-select w-auto" id="dv-table-sort2-dir"><option value="asc">&uarr;</option><option value="desc">&darr;</option></select>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm" id="dv-table"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
        </div>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
          <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="dv-table-prev">&laquo; Prev</button>
          <span id="dv-table-page-label"></span>
          <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="dv-table-next">Next &raquo;</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Columns / data quality -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-columns" role="tabpanel">
        <p>
          Confirm each column's data type &mdash; we guess automatically, but
          you can override it. <b>Constant</b> columns (only one value) and
          <b>near-unique</b> columns (almost every value is different, e.g.
          an ID) are flagged since they're rarely useful as a treatment,
          outcome or covariate. See
          <a href="/articles/data-type/" target="_blank">Data type</a> and
          <a href="/articles/cardinality/" target="_blank">Cardinality</a>
          for background.
        </p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm" id="dv-columns-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Missing</th><th>Unique values</th><th>Flags</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Univariate -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-univariate" role="tabpanel">
        <p>
          Look at one column at a time to spot bad, missing, or unexpectedly
          distributed values before you build a study. See
          <a href="/articles/exploratory-analysis/" target="_blank">Exploratory Data Analysis</a>
          for a full guide to reading these plots.
        </p>
        <div class="row mb-3">
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-uni-column">Column</label>
            <select class="form-select" id="dv-uni-column"></select>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="form-check mt-4">
              <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="dv-uni-log">
              <label class="form-check-label" for="dv-uni-log">Log y-axis</label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="dv-uni-plot" style="height:400px;"></div>
        <div id="dv-uni-stats"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bivariate -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-bivariate" role="tabpanel">
        <p>
          Look for association between two variables &mdash; a first check
          on whether a relationship you suspect (e.g. between a treatment
          and an outcome) shows up in the data. Remember that
          <a href="/articles/correlationcausality/" target="_blank">correlation isn't causation</a>:
          use this as a sanity check, not proof. Computed on a sample of up
          to 1000 rows (always including the extreme values) for speed.
        </p>
        <div class="row mb-3">
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-biv-x">Column A</label>
            <select class="form-select" id="dv-biv-x"></select>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-biv-y">Column B</label>
            <select class="form-select" id="dv-biv-y"></select>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-4" id="dv-biv-contour-toggle" hidden>
            <div class="form-check mt-4">
              <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="dv-biv-contour">
              <label class="form-check-label" for="dv-biv-contour">Show as density contour</label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="dv-biv-plot" style="height:450px;"></div>
        <div id="dv-biv-stats"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Treatment: assignment + balance + covariates, one shared widget -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-treatment" role="tabpanel">
        <p>
          Pick the variable you're considering as a <b>treatment</b> (the
          thing whose effect you want to measure) and map its values into
          <b>Control</b> and <b>Treated</b> groups &mdash; for a numeric
          column, as ranges (e.g. a threshold); for anything else, by
          assigning each value to a group. Values matching neither are
          excluded. See
          <a href="/articles/control-and-treated/" target="_blank">Control and treated groups</a>
          and <a href="/articles/positivity/" target="_blank">positivity</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="row mb-3">
          <div class="col-md-4">
            <label class="form-label" for="dv-treatment-column">Treatment column</label>
            <select class="form-select" id="dv-treatment-column"></select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="dv-treatment-widget"></div>

        <hr class="my-4" />

        <h5>Covariate balance</h5>
        <p>
          For each other column, compare its average value (numeric) or most
          common value (categorical) between your Control and Treated
          groups. Large differences are a warning sign of
          <a href="/articles/confounding/" target="_blank">confounding</a>
          &mdash; you may want that column in your causal diagram as a
          common cause. The <b>SMD</b> (standardized mean difference)
          column gives a single number for numeric covariates: as a rule of
          thumb, above 0.1 is worth a look, above 0.25 is a real imbalance.
          See <a href="/articles/covariate-balance/" target="_blank">Covariate balance</a>
          for more.
        </p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm" id="dv-covariates-table"></table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Correlations -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-correlations" role="tabpanel">
        <p>
          Pairwise correlation across all numeric columns at once &mdash; a
          quick way to spot variables that move together, which can hint at
          confounders or redundant covariates. Again,
          <a href="/articles/correlationcausality/" target="_blank">correlation isn't causation</a>.
        </p>
        <div id="dv-corr-plot" style="height:500px;"></div>
        <div class="table-responsive mt-3">
          <table class="table table-sm" id="dv-corr-table"></table>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</div>
</div>
